# macOS
*.DS_Store
.DS_Store

.vscode/

# Claude Code per-machine permission allowlist — contains the author's absolute
# /Users/<name>/... paths and legacy dir names; machine-local, must not ship.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local-only operator notes — kept out of BOTH remotes so the private→public
# mirror workflow is never advertised in the public snapshot. See PUBLISHING.md.
PUBLISHING.md

# JS test harness (Vitest) — dev-only; runtime JS stays vendored under static/js/vendor/
node_modules/

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# PyInstaller build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.spec
AppIcon.icns

# Built app bundles (dated builds)
ChatEKLD_*.app/
# Packaged distribution images (dated builds)
ChatEKLD_*.dmg

# User data — contains API keys, personal library paths, and indexed vectors.
# These live in ~/Library/Application Support/ChatEKLD/ when the app runs
# normally, but during development they may be written to the project root.
config.json
feedback.jsonl
report_types.json
llamaindex_storage/
uploads.db

# Retrieval-eval harness artifacts — these EMBED VAULT CONTENT and must never
# reach a remote. A golden set carries a `chunk_preview` excerpt of the source
# passage per query (clinical prose in the target vault) plus vault-relative
# paths; a results file carries the full ranked source-path list for every
# query x every cell. They belong under BASE_DIR/eval/, but `--out`/`--cells`
# take any path and the docs' own examples are relative (i.e. resolved against
# the repo root when run from a checkout), so prose alone is not a control —
# and this repo has a private->public mirror workflow (see PUBLISHING.md) where
# one `git add -A` would publish patient-note excerpts.
# NOTE the leading slash on /eval/: it anchors to the repo root. A bare `eval/`
# matches at ANY depth and would silently exclude the harness's own tracked
# source under tests/eval/ from every future commit (caught doing exactly that).
golden_retrieval*.json
retrieval_eval_*.json
/eval/
# Root-anchored for the same reason as /eval/ above (2026-07-29 audit): a bare
# *cells*.json matches at ANY depth and would silently swallow a future
# tracked project file that happens to carry "cells" in its name.
/*cells*.json

# Config backup left by an interrupted eval sweep (scripts/eval_retrieval.py
# writes it beside config.json so a crashed run is recoverable). Holds the
# user's real config bytes — same reason config.json itself is ignored.
config.json.evalbak

# Log files (written to ~/Library/Logs/ChatEKLD/ in production,
# but may land in the project root during development)
*.log

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.production

# Temporary files
*.tmp

# test pdf
*.pdf
*.png
!static/img/daphne.png
# README screenshots. Deliberately narrow: only this ONE directory is exempt
# from the blanket *.png above, so a stray screenshot elsewhere in the tree
# (a captured vault note, a test render) still cannot be committed by accident.
# Anything added here is published to the public mirror PERMANENTLY, git
# history included — check every image against the redaction checklist in
# PUBLISHING.md before `git add`.
#
# NOTE the location: root-level `screenshots/`, deliberately NOT `docs/`.
# The publish flow strips `docs/` wholesale (`git rm -r --cached docs/`), so a
# screenshot under docs/ would be stripped from the mirror while the README
# still linked to it — broken images on the public page.
!screenshots/*.png
*.heic

# LaTeX — deckgen emits Beamer decks (<out_dir>/<slug>/<slug>.tex) and their
# build artifacts outside the repo; the repo tracks no .tex, so keep stray
# generated decks and compile by-products (e.g. from a CLI --out run) out of git.
# Use `git add -f` if a template ever needs to live in the repo.
*.tex
*.aux
*.nav
*.snm
*.toc
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk